      "dom_id": "question-102233",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=2{x}^{2}-2$ whose tangent has a slope of $2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-2.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2x-0 \\\\  & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=2$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $2$ at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
